        "label": "Resolve each displacement",
        "marks": 2,
        "mark_note": "Components",
        "lines": [
          "Take east as x and north as y.",
          "North-east and north-west are at 45°,",
          "and 10√2 cos 45° = 10√2 / √2 = 10. So:",
          {
            "text": "s₁ = 10 i + 10 j   (north-east)",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "s₂ = 10 j          (north)",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "s₃ = −10 i + 10 j  (north-west)",
            "style": "eq"
          }
        ],
        "margin_note": "Two marks sit on these three lines. The only work is 10√2 × (1/√2) = 10 — show it once.",
        "why": "Directions like north-east cannot be added as words. Turning each leg into i and j components turns the walk into simple addition.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing 10√2 for a component instead of 10.",
          "Giving north-west a positive x component."
        ],
        "recall": {
          "credit": "say_it",
          "must_convey": "That each displacement is resolved: 10i+10j, 10j, and −10i+10j.",
          "accept": [
            "resolve each displacement into components",
            "ten root two at forty five gives ten and ten",
            "north west lo minus ten i plus ten j",
            "east x axis north y axis teeskunta"
